{
  "_comment": "Illustrative external enterprise group (ADR-BCP-018 sections 36, 44, 54). No entry in the Shared legal-entity registry is required. All identifiers are opaque and Control Plane-minted (section 12): the human-readable name, 'Acme' branding and the company registration number live in names and registration_identifiers, never in ids. Holdings, Foods and Logistics are VERIFIED only through evidence review (evidence_references + verified_by + verified_at). Retail is an applicant claim that has not been reviewed (UNVERIFIED), and its claimed ownership is CONFLICTED because two sources disagree; both must fail closed for consequential decisions. Every organisation is EXTERNAL_CLIENT; the OWNS graph confers no cross-tenant access, and the shared PlatformAccount confers no authorization. Acme Foods signs in through two IAM realms (production and an EU-residency realm), so it has two ACTIVE IamOrganisationReferences, plus a RETIRED one from an earlier realm that never resolves (section 65). The admission examples onboard Acme Logistics after an approved decision: it declares that Acme Holdings owns it (recorded PENDING_REVIEW, never verified by admission), the reviewer verifies its legal identity and places it in the existing Acme account; a second applicant whose registration number matches Acme Foods is QUARANTINED rather than merged (sections 99-100).",
